Modifications (as required by Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))
--------------------------------------------------------------
1. Added module `desktopApp`: the Windows entry point (Compose Desktop window,
   packaging via jpackage/MSI, app icon, window state, settings page,
   session restore, autostart).
2. Added Android/JVM `jvmShared` source set in `:app` and moved the original
   Android sources into it, so the same UI and business logic build for both
   platforms; added `expect/actual` capability declarations
   (`AppCapabilities`, `PlatformStarter`, `OcrSupport`, `ClipBoardHelper`,
   `CalendarWriter`, `LanguageHelper`, `AppAssets`, ...).
3. Extracted platform page dispatch (`ui/nav/PlatformScreens.*`) and added
   `logic/platform/PlatformFeatures.kt`, which hides pages that only exist on
   Android.
4. Replaced Android-only implementations on desktop: in-app WebView becomes the
   system browser, system-calendar writes become an `.ics` export, QR codes are
   drawn with zxing on a Compose Canvas, PNG icons are read from classpath
   resources instead of APK assets.
5. Added a cross-platform preferences store, and desktop-specific pages
   (appearance settings, settings list).
6. Replaced the app icon with new artwork (red field, white "HFUT" lettering).
7. Added verification tasks under `:desktopApp` (offscreen render, login probe,
   ICS export, icon lookup, feature filtering, session/autostart probe).

